<figcaption id="caption-attachment-124646" class="wp-caption-text">Image Credit: Apple Inc.</figcaption></figure>
<h2 class="p1">CPU Architecture: Identical Core Structure</h2>
<p class="p1">M5 Pro and M5 Max both feature the same 18-core CPU configuration:</p>
<ul>
<li class="p1">6 super cores (highest single-thread performance)</li>
<li class="p1">12 performance cores optimized for multithreaded workloads</li>
</ul>
<p class="p1">The super cores represent Apple’s fastest CPU core design to date, featuring improved front-end bandwidth, new cache hierarchy, and enhanced branch prediction.</p>
<p class="p1">In multithreaded tasks, both chips deliver up to 30 percent performance gains compared to the previous generation and up to 2.5x higher multithreaded performance compared to M1 Pro and M1 Max.</p>
<p class="p1">Where they begin to diverge is in GPU scale and memory bandwidth.</p>
<h2 class="p1">GPU Performance and AI Compute</h2>
<p class="p1">The GPU is the primary differentiator between M5 Pro and M5 Max.</p>
<h4 class="p1">M5 Pro:</h4>
<ul>
<li class="p1">Up to 20 GPU cores</li>
<li class="p1">Neural Accelerator in each GPU core</li>
<li class="p1">Over 4x peak GPU AI compute compared to the previous generation</li>
<li class="p1">Up to 35 percent graphics uplift in ray-tracing workloads vs prior generation</li>
</ul>
<h4 class="p1">M5 Max:</h4>
<ul>
<li class="p1">Up to 40 GPU cores</li>
<li class="p1">Neural Accelerator in each GPU core</li>
<li class="p1">Over 4x peak GPU AI compute compared to the previous generation</li>
<li class="p1">Up to 30 percent graphics uplift in ray-tracing workloads vs prior generation</li>
</ul>
<p class="p1">M5 Max effectively doubles the maximum GPU core count compared to M5 Pro.</p>
<h4 class="p1">This makes it better suited for:</h4>
<ul>
<li class="p1">Complex 3D rendering</li>
<li class="p1">Advanced visual effects</li>
<li class="p1">High-resolution multi-stream video editing</li>
<li class="p1">Large AI model training</li>
</ul>
<p class="p1">Both chips support hardware-accelerated mesh shading and third-generation ray tracing, but the raw GPU scale advantage places M5 Max at the top tier for GPU-heavy workflows.</p>
