<p class="p1">Memory Bandwidth</p>
</td>
<td>
<p class="p1">Up to 307GB/s</p>
</td>
<td>
<p class="p1">Up to 614GB/s</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>
<p class="p1">Media Engine</p>
</td>
<td>
<p class="p1">H.264, HEVC, AV1 decode, ProRes encode/decode</p>
</td>
<td>
<p class="p1">H.264, HEVC, AV1 decode, ProRes encode/decode</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>
<p class="p1">Thunderbolt Support</p>
</td>
<td>
<p class="p1">Thunderbolt 5 (dedicated controller per port)</p>
</td>
<td>
<p class="p1">Thunderbolt 5 (dedicated controller per port)</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>
<p class="p1">Best For</p>
</td>
<td>
<p class="p1">Advanced pro workflows, 4K editing, development, data modeling</p>
</td>
<td>
<p class="p1">3D animation, 8K workflows, large AI models, simulations</p>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p class="p1">For most demanding pro workflows, M5 Pro delivers significant gains. For extreme GPU-intensive and AI-driven environments, M5 Max unlocks the highest ceiling Apple currently offers in a pro laptop platform.</p>
